From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LeavesMC <noreply@leavesmc.org>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Optimize jigsaw structure layout

Vanilla maintains the free space of a jigsaw generation pass as a `VoxelShape`
built by repeatedly joining/subtracting integer-aligned `AABB`s. Every placement
test and every placement update therefore rebuilds a shape object whose size
grows with the number of already placed pieces, which dominates the cost of
`JigsawPlacement.Placer#tryPlacingChildren` for large structures (ancient city,
trial chambers).

This patch keeps exactly the same geometry but stores it in an octree: the
original maximum-distance `AABB` becomes the octree boundary and each placed
piece is registered as an occupied box, so containment checks and registration
become bounded-depth lookups instead of full shape reconstructions.

Two things are deliberately *not* changed, because either would alter world
generation:

* The random number sequence. Every vanilla call that consumes the shared
  `WorldgenRandom` is still performed, in the same order; when a rotation loop
  is skipped because that pool element was already fully tried, the skipped
  `getShuffledJigsawBlocks` calls are replayed first so the RNG stream stays
  aligned.
* The layout itself. Both representations describe the same integer-aligned box
  set, so generated structures are identical to vanilla.

The octree is carried by a marker `VoxelShape` (`TrojanVoxelShape`) that holds
no voxel data. Paper's collision patch only initialises `cachedShapeData` from
`CubeVoxelShape`/`ArrayVoxelShape`/`SliceShape`, and an uninitialised shape is
silently treated as *empty* by `CollisionUtil` - which would yield wrong results
instead of an error. Every consumer of the free-space shape is therefore routed
through `StructureLayoutBridge`, which checks for the marker with `instanceof`
and otherwise evaluates the verbatim vanilla expression.

Everything is gated behind `performance.structure-layout-optimizer` and
`performance.structure-layout-deduplicate-template-pool`. With both disabled the
original statements are evaluated verbatim, so behaviour is bit-for-bit vanilla.

This patch is Powered by StructureLayoutOptimizer(https://github.com/TelepathicGrunt/StructureLayoutOptimizer)

This patch is based on the following mixins:
* "telepathicgrunt/structure_layout_optimizer/mixins/JigsawPlacementMixin.java"
* "telepathicgrunt/structure_layout_optimizer/mixins/JigsawPlacementPlacerMixin.java"
